4. BFS + Maximum Value Among Shortest Paths

Now each node has a value:
int[] value;

We want: Among all shortest paths, what is the maximum total value?

Add: int[] best = new int[n + 1];

Code:

void bfs(int start, ArrayList<Integer>[] graph,
         int[] value, int n) {

    boolean[] visited = new boolean[n + 1];
    int[] level = new int[n + 1];
    int[] best = new int[n + 1];

    Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<>();

    q.add(start);

    visited[start] = true;
    level[start] = 0;
    best[start] = value[start];

    while(!q.isEmpty()) {

        int node = q.poll();
        for(int neighbour : graph[node]) {
            // First time reaching neighbour
            if(!visited[neighbour]) {
                visited[neighbour] = true;
                level[neighbour] = level[node] + 1;
                best[neighbour] = best[node] + value[neighbour];
                q.add(neighbour);
            }
            // Another shortest path
            else if(level[neighbour] == level[node] + 1) {
                best[neighbour] = Math.max(best[neighbour],best[node] + value[neighbour]);
            }
        }
    }
}

Core idea
level → shortest distance
ways → number of shortest paths
best → maximum value among shortest paths
